# Windows StickLLM USB flash

Windows does not like Linux-flashed USB keys. StickLLM isohybrid often has **no drive letter** after flash; Windows still sees the disk. Do **not** assume the stick is missing when there is no letter.

## Prefer

1. Elevated `C:\Python314\python.exe` + `out/safe-flash-samsung-auth.py` (Clear-Disk + FSCTL lock/dismount + WriteFile). Proven FLASH_OK path.
2. Fallback: **Rufus DD Image** mode.

## Avoid

- Naive PowerShell `FileStream` raw write → Access Denied even when elevated.
- `Set-Disk -IsOffline` on removable Samsung sticks.

## Remember

- No letter ≠ missing USB. Confirm with disk number / size / bus (e.g. Get-Disk), not Explorer.
- Only flash when the user explicitly asks; never overwrite a shipping release under an existing name.
